    "reading": "M2 grew 4.4x; consumer prices and wages rose under half as fast; assets absorbed the gap and gold/silver exceeded it. Monetary expansion is the leading candidate mechanism and is strongly ASSOCIATED with the asset-inflation term - but no single money aggregate explains the cross-asset dispersion (gold ran ~2x M2, homes ~0.7x), and confounders (globalisation goods-disinflation, rates, financialisation, EM central-bank gold buying, real earnings growth) are uncontrolled. Association, not proof of cause."
